  77:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *
  78:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** * \brief
  79:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  Establishes synchronized communication with the Tuner application.
  80:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *
  81:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** * \details
  82:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  This function is used to establish synchronized communication between the 
  83:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  CapSense component and Tuner application (or other host controllers).
  84:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  This function should be called periodically in the application program loop 
  85:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  to serve the Tuner application (or host controller) requests and commands. 
  86:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  In most cases, the best place to call this function is after processing and 
  87:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  before next scanning. 
  88:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  
  89:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  If this function is absent in the application program, then communication is 
  90:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  asynchronous and the following disadvantages are applicable:
  91:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *    - The raw counts displayed in the tuner may be filtered and/or unfiltered 
  92:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *      firmware and as a result, noise and SNR measurements will not be 
  93:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *      accurate.
  94:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *    - The Tuner may read the sensor data such as raw counts from a scan 
  95:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *      multiple times, as a result, noise and SNR measurement will not be 
  96:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *      accurate.
  97:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *    - The Tuner and host controller should not change the component parameters 
  98:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *      via the tuner interface. Changing the component parameters via the tuner 
  99:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *      interface in the async mode will result in abnormal behavior from the 
 100:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *      component.
 101:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  
 102:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  Note that calling this function is not mandatory for the application, but 
 103:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  required only to synchronize the communication with the host controller or 
 104:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  tuner application.
 105:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *
 106:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** * \return
 107:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  In some cases, the application program may need to know if the component was
 108:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *  re-initialized. The return indicates if a restart command was executed or not: 
 109:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *    - CapSense_STATUS_RESTART_DONE based on a received command, the 
 110:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *      component was restarted.
 111:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *    -  CapSense_STATUS_RESTART_NONE, no restart was executed by this 
 112:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Tuner.c **** *      function.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lenovo\AppData\Local\Temp\ccXJBRfc.s 			page 4


